join "Mama Zulu" left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Mama Zulu\: The Dube girl's machine has been moved.
- Naledi's?
	Hope: Naledi's?
	Mama Zulu\: It sat in that trunk three years. Now it is out and there is oil on the wheel.
	Mama Zulu\: I walked over on Sunday. I did not ask her about it.
	- What did you talk about?
		Hope: What did you talk about?
		Mama Zulu\: Nothing. I brought bread and I sat for an hour.
	- Why not ask?
		Hope: Why not ask?
		Mama Zulu\: Because she would have said she was fine, and then she would have had to keep saying it.
		Mama Zulu\: This way she did not have to say anything.
